### Item 1 | HPSMPOC-329 (B549-1): the digit and punctuation neighbours of the exact numbers (`web/src/server/mock/attribution-preview.test.ts` only)
**Done-when:** (a) a table-driven row with **every digit 0 to 9 on each side of 777 and of 4321** (10 x 2 x 2 = 40 cells) expecting `leaksExactNumber(text)` = false; (b) a table-driven row with **every printable ASCII punctuation character (the 32 characters 0x21-0x2F, 0x3A-0x40, 0x5B-0x60, 0x7B-0x7E) on each side of 777 and of 4321** (32 x 2 x 2 = 128 cells) expecting true, plus the space (0x20) on each side expecting true (a space joins nothing); the existing 8-cell letter/underscore/dot/hyphen table stays untouched. The two sets are built from the character ranges by program (a loop over code points), not typed by hand, and a self-check row asserts the sets have 10 and 32 members (so a typo cannot silently shrink them). A text in a cell is the bare `${c}${n}` or `${n}${c}` (no id, no timestamp), so the `ENGAGEMENT_ID` and `ISO_TIMESTAMP` removals cannot change the verdict.
**Watch:** a punctuation cell must not accidentally form an id or an ISO timestamp (it cannot: the texts are two to five characters); if a cell reads differently from what the ruling in the file header says (only a digit exempts), that is a finding to report, not a row to bend.
**Mutants (on a SCRATCH copy of the test file in the mutant tree; anchor count 1; sha256 before/after; byte-equal restore), each killed by a NAMED new row or reported SURVIVES:** `O-M9-narrow` (`(?<![0-5])(?:777|4321)(?![0-5])`); `O-M9-narrow-left` and `O-M9-narrow-right` (one side only); a digit-class mutant for EACH digit d in 0-9 (the digit d no longer exempts, on the left, then on the right: 20 mutants, generated by program, each must be killed by the digit table); `W-L-slash-plus` (`(?<![\d/+])`) and its right-side twin; and, by program, one mutant per printable ASCII punctuation character c that exempts c on the left, and one that exempts c on the right (64 mutants: each must be killed by the punctuation table). Controls: c0 (unmutated), c1 (a trailing comment), c2 (an equivalent whitespace change) read 0 red with ran > 0; one control that the OLD rows alone (the file at main) leave `O-M9-narrow` and `W-L-slash-plus` SURVIVING (this proves the new rows are what kills them: it reproduces the gate's two survivors).

